(Title) Tj
T*
(Effectiveness of a Standalone Digital Platform for Postpartum Depression: A Randomized) Tj
T*
(Comparative Effectiveness Study) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Postpartum depression affects a substantial proportion of new mothers and limits) Tj
T*
(engagement with usual treatment. We randomized 264 postpartum women to receive either a) Tj
T*
(standalone mobile application designed to address depressive symptoms or an active control) Tj
T*
(intervention. Both groups had access to routine postpartum care. Depressive symptoms were) Tj
T*
(assessed using standardized depression screening tools, and functional capacity was) Tj
T*
(measured using clinician-rated global impression scales at treatment endpoint. The) Tj
T*
(application group demonstrated greater improvement in depression scores compared to) Tj
T*
(controls \(mean reduction 8.2 points vs 4.1 points, p = 0.001, Cohen d = 0.55\). Functional) Tj
T*
(impairment also improved more substantially in the intervention group \(mean 1.8-point) Tj
T*
(improvement vs 0.9-point improvement on clinical global impression, p = 0.008\). Treatment) Tj
T*
(effects were observed across diverse demographic subgroups. User engagement with the) Tj
T*
(platform was variable; approximately 58% of participants engaged with core features at) Tj
T*
(least twice weekly. The intervention was well-tolerated with high acceptability ratings.) Tj
T*
(These findings suggest that well-designed standalone digital interventions can) Tj
T*
(meaningfully reduce depressive symptoms in the postpartum period.) Tj
ET
